(library
 (name mgen_nn)
 ; The common parts of the neural-net sources. Each of the three eras holds a model in two
 ; layers — the JAX model and its integer twin above the seam, the [Model] and the circuit
 ; below it — and what is one thing across the eras stands here one time: the units, the
 ; fixed-point rules the circuits read and the tables they elaborate. NOTHING HERE
 ; QUANTIZES and nothing here draws in float: those are rules of a checkpoint and of a
 ; sampling policy, and both live above the seam with the twins. What only rhymes between
 ; the eras — the op vocabularies, the schedules, the parameter structures — stays in the
 ; era libraries.
 ;
 ; THE OP/SCHEDULE QUESTION IS CLOSED, and the op/schedule round closed it by measuring.
 ; The draw of the chain and L3's compiler were not rhyme: they were one text under two
 ; module names, and they are [Sampler] and [Program] now, both netlist-identical. THE
 ; VOCABULARIES STAY IN THE ERAS: of the nine constructors the two [Op.t] share, three
 ; differ in a field, thus the true common set is [where], [tensor], [Embed], [Accumulate]
 ; and the four draw ops -- and the draw ops already meet in [Sampler]. That is rhyme. So
 ; is L4, where ten lines differ by the ring era four keeps and era five has not.
 (libraries base core stdio hardcaml hardcaml_waveterm nx nx.io mgen_core)
 (flags
  (:standard -open Mgen_core))
 (inline_tests
  (flags
   (:standard -source-tree-root .)))
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_hardcaml ppx_expect ppx_compare ppx_enumerate ppx_sexp_conv)))
